{"type":"text","timestamp":1794565305453,"sessionID":"ses_e2b969798ffeOhgXFij3UsleJR","part":{"id":"prt_1d46d6283002nJ6IHQJBZ4AbvQ","sessionID":"ses_e2b969798ffeOhgXFij3UsleJR","messageID":"msg_1d46d4ba8001eig4r7AnxjzU7O","type":"text","text":"T021 is implemented and verified.\n\n## Files written\n\n**`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`**\n- Guard changed to `command && (!alreadyOffered.has(command) || (topOnly && index === 0))`.\n- Added the comment explaining that a top-only caller renders the head alone, so a command carried only by a lower row would never reach the reader.\n\n**`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts`**\n- Added a case after `never offers one command through both its own row and the owning hub` that reads `cmd-create-agent-plain-tune-01` from `scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl` by id, asserts `split` is `tune`, mocks the `sk-doc` single-mode route to `/create:agent`, and checks: with `compiledRouteTopOnly` the first row is `sk-doc` carrying `/create:agent` and `create:agent` still ranks later; without it the `sk-doc` row carries no command.\n\n## Verify output\n\n`V tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` (run as `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run ...` in `$ADV`):\n\n```\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  7 passed (7)\nV_EXIT:0\n```\n\n`TC` (`npm run typecheck`):\n```\n> ../../system-spec-kit/node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit --composite false -p tsconfig.build.json\nTC_EXIT:0\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- I confirmed the new case pins the change: with the old guard restored temporarily, it fails with `expected undefined to be '/create:agent'` (1 failed | 6 passed). That self-check briefly left the handler in its old state when a restore trap ran from the wrong directory; I re-applied the edit, then re-ran both verifies from the final state (output above) and read the scoped diff to confirm the final content.\n- `advisor-status.vitest.ts` shows as modified in `git status`, but that is another worker's file and I did not touch it.\n- `sk-doc` is first for that corpus prompt, so no `[B]` marking was needed.\n- Checkbox left unticked as instructed.","time":{"start":1794565300867,"end":1794565305453}}}
